# hopsesh reference (version {{.Version}})

## Commands Claude may run without asking

| Command | Does |
|---|---|
| `{{.Bin}} ls --json [--host M] [--repo R] [--live] [--no-git] [--limit N]` | list sessions on allowed machines |
| `{{.Bin}} show <ref> --json` | one session's details |
| `{{.Bin}} plan <ref> --json [flags]` | what moving it would do; never writes |
| `{{.Bin}} hosts --json` | discovered machines and whether each is allowed |
| `{{.Bin}} doctor [machine] --json` | SSH, host trust, Claude Code version, Remote Control, skill |
| `{{.Bin}} version` | the installed version |

## Needs the user's yes first

`{{.Bin}} pull <ref> --json --yes [flags]` moves the session. `{{.Bin}} undo <id>` reverses a move.

## pull and plan flags

| Flag | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `--clone` | clone the repository into the repos folder if it is not here |
| `--to <dir>` | resume in this directory instead of matching the repository |
| `--worktree auto\|create\|main` | recreate the session's worktree (auto), always use one, or use the main checkout |
| `--fork` | the old session keeps running; both continue (default: hand off) |
| `--rc` | start the moved session with Remote Control on |
| `--notify` | the moved session tells the old one where the work went (both on Remote Control) |
| `--redact` | redact likely secrets in the copy |
| `--other-account` | this machine uses a different Claude account (drops signed reasoning) |
| `--memory` | also merge the project's auto-memory folder |
| `--stop-local` | quit a copy of this session running on this machine first |
| `--keep-both` / `--replace` | when the copy here changed too: bring this one in separately / replace it |
| `--no-sync` | leave the checkout here alone (default: fetch, and fast-forward when clean) |
| `--no-mark` | do not title the copy left behind "↪ moved to <this machine>" |
| `--push` | push the source branch's unpushed commits first (by default they are fetched straight from the other machine) |

## JSON

`plan --json` prints the plan. `pull --json --yes` prints
`{"plan": …, "result": …, "resumeCommand": "…", "argv": […]}`. Useful plan fields:
`sessionId`, `title`, `sourceHost`, `targetCwd`, `repo.action`, `repo.localPath`,
`repo.worktree`, `repo.unpushed`, `repo.dirty`, `sync`, `mark` (`now`, `when-stopped`, `off`),
`conflict`, `warnings`, `blockers`. Result fields: `syncNote`, `sync.state`, `pushed`,
`pushError`, `mark` (`done`, `pending`, `off`, `failed`), `markError`, `undoId`.

## Permissions and the sandbox

hopsesh reads other machines over SSH and writes into `~/.claude/projects`, which Claude Code's
sandbox does not allow. If the user runs Claude Code with the sandbox on, they can add to
`~/.claude/settings.json`:

```json
{ "sandbox": { "excludedCommands": ["{{.Bin}} ls *", "{{.Bin}} show *", "{{.Bin}} plan *", "{{.Bin}} pull *"] } }
```

`{{.Bin}} skill install --add-rules` can also add permission rules: read-only commands allowed,
and `pull`, `undo` and `import` always asking.
